        <body>
            <div xml:id="d91">

                <pb facs="0165" n="158" sameAs="frus:frus1894Nicaragua/pg158"/>

                <head>No. 91.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Herbert to Mr. Gresham.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Navy Department</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1894-08-15"><hi rendition="#italic">August 15,
                        1894</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inclose herewith copies
                    of two communications, both dated Bluefields, Nicaragua, July 21 and 25,
                    respectively received from Commander Charles O’Neil, U. S. N., commanding the U.
                    S. S. <hi rendition="#italic">Marblehead</hi>, relating to the political
                    situation in Nicaragua.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">H. A. Herbert</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Secretary of the Navy.</hi></signed></closer>








